#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/basics/teleporter/quest.tres
msgid "Teleporters"
msgstr "Teletransportadores"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/basics/teleporter/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn how to use teleporters to go from scene to scene or between two points "
"in the same scene."
msgstr ""
"Aprende a usar teletransportadores para ir de una escena a otra o entre dos "
"puntos en la misma escena."

#: scenes/dev/basics/teleporter/teleporter_test_1.tscn
msgid "Continue walking to teleport to another scene!"
msgstr "¡Sigue caminando para teletransportarte a otra escena!"

#: scenes/dev/basics/teleporter/teleporter_test_1.tscn
msgid ""
"Teleporting while walking east uses a \"Right to Left Wipe\" transition. "
"When you return, notice how the transition changes to reflect the direction "
"you walk!"
msgstr ""
"Al teletransportarte caminando hacia el este se usa una transición \"Right "
"to Left Wipe\". Cuando regreses, ¡fíjate cómo cambia la transición para "
"reflejar la dirección en la que caminas!"

#: scenes/dev/basics/teleporter/teleporter_test_2.tscn
msgid "Teleportation can also exist between two points in the same scene!"
msgstr ""
"¡La teletransportación también puede existir entre dos puntos de la misma "
"escena!"

#: scenes/dev/basics/teleporter/teleporter_test_2.tscn
msgid ""
"We only give a teleporter a transition if the spawn point is not visible "
"when using it."
msgstr ""
"Solo le damos una transición a un teletransportador si el spawn point no "
"está visible al usarlo."

#: scenes/dev/basics/teleporter/teleporter_test_2.tscn
msgid ""
"Each teleporter can reference a SpawnPoint as a target to move the Player "
"to. Add a spawn_point.tscn to your scene and then select it from the "
"teleporter's \"Spawn Point Path\" dropdown in the inspector."
msgstr ""
"Cada teletransportador puede referenciar un SpawnPoint como destino para "
"mover al Player. Agrega un spawn_point.tscn a tu escena y luego selecciónalo "
"en la lista \"Spawn Point Path\" del teletransportador, en el inspector."

#: scenes/dev/basics/teleporter/teleporter_test_2.tscn
msgid "You can walk back the way you came to return to the first scene!"
msgstr "¡Puedes volver por donde viniste para regresar a la primera escena!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/quest.tres
msgid "Visuals"
msgstr "Visuales"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn how to order TileMapLayers, create fake perspective, and maintain "
"logical y-sorting of sprites in your quests."
msgstr ""
"Aprende a ordenar TileMapLayers, crear perspectivas falsas y mantener un y-"
"sorting lógico en los sprites de tus misiones."

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid ""
"In the world of Threadbare, we want a consistent perspective where sprites "
"are layered in a logical order."
msgstr ""
"En el mundo de Threadbare queremos una perspectiva consistente, donde los "
"sprites se superpongan en un orden lógico."

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid ""
"For example, if you walk behind this house, it should appear in front of you!"
msgstr ""
"Por ejemplo, si caminas detrás de esta casa, ¡debería verse por delante de "
"ti!\n"

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid ""
"For nodes that appear \"on the ground\", we like to group them under a "
"Node2D with Y Sort Enabled."
msgstr ""
"Para los nodos que aparecen \"en el suelo\", nos gusta agruparlos bajo un "
"Node2D con Y Sort Enabled."

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid "Otherwise you get weird visuals! (Try walking right behind this house)"
msgstr "Si no, ¡se ve todo raro! (Prueba caminar justo detrás de esta casa)"

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid ""
"We can also create the illusion of elevated cliffs with the elevation_2.tres "
"and shadow.tres tilesets."
msgstr ""
"También podemos crear la ilusión de acantilados elevados con los tilesets "
"elevation_2.tres y shadow.tres."

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid "Don't be afraid to add more TileMapLayers!"
msgstr "¡No tengas miedo de agregar más TileMapLayers!"

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid ""
"Be careful with the perspective of elevation. The foam should not be visible "
"off the back."
msgstr ""
"Ten cuidado con la perspectiva de la elevación. La espuma no debería verse "
"por detrás."

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid ""
"This back tile should have an alternate water tile (no collision) to round "
"out the corner!"
msgstr ""
"¡Este tile de atrás debería tener un tile de agua alternativo (sin colisión) "
"para redondear la esquina!"

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid ""
"The alternative tiles make it possible to walk above water and stone when "
"using bridges."
msgstr ""
"Los tiles alternativos hacen posible caminar por encima del agua y la piedra "
"al usar puentes."

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid "Head this way to see an interactive Y-Sort example."
msgstr "Ve por aquí para ver un ejemplo interactivo de Y-Sort."

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid "Use the foam_2.tres tileset whenever water contacts land."
msgstr "Usa el tileset foam_2.tres siempre que el agua toque la tierra."

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid "Enable Y-Sorting"
msgstr "Activar Y-Sorting"

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid "Disable Y-Sorting"
msgstr "Desactivar Y-Sorting"

#: scenes/dev/basics/visuals/visuals_test.tscn
msgid ""
"Shadows under bridges should reflect elevation. Make sure that the start and "
"end points are consistent."
msgstr ""
"Las sombras bajo los puentes deben reflejar la elevación. Asegúrate de que "
"los puntos de inicio y de fin sean consistentes."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character name
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue
msgctxt "dialogue"
msgid "Basics Elder"
msgstr "Anciano ConceptosBásicos"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Basics Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue:3
msgid "[[Hi|Hello|Greetings]], StoryWeaver. Welcome to Dev Archipelago!"
msgstr ""
"[[Hola|Buenas|Saludos]], StoryWeaver. Te doy la bienvenida al Archipiélago "
"Dev!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Basics Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue:4
msgid "This is a place of creativity, play, and experimentation!"
msgstr "¡Este es un lugar de creatividad, juego y experimentación!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Basics Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue:5
msgid ""
"While I can't explain all of what happens here, I invite you to learn about "
"the basics of our unraveling world!"
msgstr ""
"Aunque no puedo explicar todo lo que sucede aquí, ¡te invito a conocer las "
"cosas básicas de nuestro descosido mundo!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Basics Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue:9
msgid ""
"Feel free to explore these islands, however these quests might be a helpful "
"way to start!"
msgstr ""
"Siéntete libre de explorar estas islas, ¡estas misiones podrían ser una "
"buena manera de empezar!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Basics Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue:10
msgid ""
"Explore and have fun! I hope to see you again if you need to relearn the "
"basics."
msgstr ""
"¡Explora y diviértete! Espero verte de nuevo si necesitas repasar los "
"conceptos básicos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Basics Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue:11
msgid ""
"The people of Threadbare are counting on you. Your understanding of our "
"world is necessary for its survival!"
msgstr ""
"Los habitantes de Threadbare cuentan contigo. ¡Tu comprensión de nuestro "
"mundo es fundamental para su supervivencia!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Basics Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue:13
msgid ""
"Excellent choice, your training will surely help with your world-saving "
"efforts."
msgstr ""
"Excelente elección, el entrenamiento sin duda te ayudará en tus esfuerzos de "
"salvar el mundo."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Basics Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue:14
msgid ""
"Ah, those! Capable of such ingenuity. To do what? I can't quite remember..."
msgstr "¡Ah, esos! Tan ingeniosos. ¿Para qué servían? No lo recuerdo bien..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Basics Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_basics_elder.dialogue:15
msgid "I'm confident you will know how to use this on your journey."
msgstr "Estoy seguro de que sabrás cómo usar esto en tu viaje."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character name
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue
msgctxt "dialogue"
msgid "Enemy Interaction Elder"
msgstr "Anciano InteraccionesDeEnemigos"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Enemy Interaction Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue:3
msgid ""
"The animals can get jumpy when the void acts up... We will try to wrangle "
"them back to safety!"
msgstr ""
"Los animales pueden ponerse nerviosos cuando el Void se alborota... "
"¡Intentaremos llevarlos de vuelta a un lugar seguro!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Enemy Interaction Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue:4
msgid ""
"It's a good idea to learn how to interact with all sorts of creatures in "
"Threadbare, some friendly and some not so much."
msgstr ""
"Es buena idea aprender a interactuar con todo tipo de criaturas en "
"Threadbare, algunas amigables y otras no tanto."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Enemy Interaction Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue:5
msgid "Don't let your guard down during these quests!"
msgstr "¡No bajes la guardia durante estas misiones!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Enemy Interaction Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue:9
msgid ""
"I understand, it took me a while to be comfortable navigating StoryVore "
"caves."
msgstr ""
"Lo entiendo, me llevó un tiempo sentirme cómodo navegando por las cuevas de "
"los StoryVore."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Enemy Interaction Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue:10
msgid "This is a good place to test your speed and agility when you need it!"
msgstr ""
"¡Este es un buen lugar para poner a prueba tu velocidad y agilidad cuando "
"las necesites!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Enemy Interaction Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue:11
msgid ""
"When you're ready, these quests will give you a better idea of what you're "
"up against!"
msgstr ""
"Cuando quieras probarlas, ¡estas misiones te darán una mejor idea de a qué "
"te enfrentas!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Enemy Interaction Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue:13
msgid "Wow, you're brave! Good luck out there."
msgstr "¡Qué valiente! Mucha suerte por allá."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Enemy Interaction Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue:14
msgid "Move quickly and use hiding spots to your advantage!"
msgstr "¡Muévete rápido y aprovecha los escondites a tu favor!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Enemy Interaction Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_enemy_interaction_elder.dialogue:15
msgid "Don't forget to pay attention to how creatures move along paths!"
msgstr ""
"¡No olvides prestar atención a cómo se desplazan las criaturas por los "
"caminos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character name
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_grapple_elder.dialogue
msgctxt "dialogue"
msgid "Grapple Elder"
msgstr "EnganchAnciano"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Grapple Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_grapple_elder.dialogue:3
msgid "Welcome to my grapple island, StoryWeaver."
msgstr "Te doy la bienvenida a mi enganchada isla, StoryWeaver."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Grapple Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_grapple_elder.dialogue:4
msgid ""
"Did you know that you can hook on to more than just pins? And how do you "
"reckon that sheep got a different string?"
msgstr ""
"¿Sabías que puedes engancharte a algo más que a alfileres? ¿Y cómo crees que "
"esa oveja consiguió una cuerda diferente?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Grapple Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_grapple_elder.dialogue:5
msgid ""
"Perhaps these quests may offer you some inspiration on how your grapple can "
"be used!"
msgstr ""
"¡Quizás estas misiones te sirvan de inspiración sobre cómo utilizar tu "
"gancho!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Grapple Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_grapple_elder.dialogue:9
msgid ""
"Oh well, be sure to return when you are ready to learn about all that is "
"hookable."
msgstr ""
"En fin, asegúrate de volver cuando quieras aprender sobre todo lo que se "
"puede enganchar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Grapple Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_grapple_elder.dialogue:10
msgid ""
"There are many other islands here with fun to be had! Take your time "
"exploring."
msgstr ""
"¡Aquí hay muchas otras islas donde divertirse! Tómate tu tiempo para "
"explorarlas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Grapple Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_grapple_elder.dialogue:12
msgid ""
"Nice one! I'd be trying this too, if I could only get my string back from "
"those woolly rascals..."
msgstr ""
"¡Buena elección! Yo también la probaría, si tan solo pudiera recuperar mi "
"cuerda de esos pícaros lanudos..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Grapple Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_grapple_elder.dialogue:13
msgid "Good luck with your experimenting!"
msgstr "¡Buena suerte con tus experimentos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character name
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_intro_islander.dialogue
msgctxt "dialogue"
msgid "Imagine Islander"
msgstr "Isleño ImaginaCosas"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Imagine Islander
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_intro_islander.dialogue:3
msgid "Hi StoryWeaver!"
msgstr "¡Hola StoryWeaver!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Imagine Islander
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_intro_islander.dialogue:4
msgid "Let me give you some advice for exploring the archipelago."
msgstr "Déjame darte algunas recomendaciones para explorar el archipiélago."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Imagine Islander
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_intro_islander.dialogue:5
msgid ""
"Whenever you get lost trying out some new mechanics, just open up the game "
"menu and click \"Abandon Quest\". It will bring you right back to the island."
msgstr ""
"Si alguna vez te pierdes mientras pruebas nuevas mecánicas, simplemente abre "
"el menú del juego y haz clic en \"Abandonar misión\". Eso te traerá de "
"regreso a la isla."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Imagine Islander
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_intro_islander.dialogue:6
msgid ""
"If you stumble across something you like, open the debug settings from the "
"options menu and click \"Open Current Scene In Editor\" to take a closer "
"look at how the scene works."
msgstr ""
"Si encuentras algo que te guste, abre la configuración de depuración desde "
"el menú de opciones y haz clic en \"Abrir escena actual en el editor\" para "
"ver más de cerca cómo se ve la escena."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Imagine Islander
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_intro_islander.dialogue:7
msgid ""
"One more thing. Sometimes helpful information appears in the editor but "
"isn't included on the signs. In the editor, you can right-click a node and "
"choose \"Open Documentation\" to get more details."
msgstr ""
"Una cosa más. A veces aparece información útil en el editor, pero no se "
"incluye en los letreros. En el editor, puedes hacer clic con el botón "
"derecho en un nodo y seleccionar \"Abrir documentación\" para obtener más "
"detalles."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Imagine Islander
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_intro_islander.dialogue:8
msgid "Good luck and let your imagination lead you!"
msgstr "¡Buena suerte y que te guíe la imaginación!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character name
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_level_design_elder.dialogue
msgctxt "dialogue"
msgid "Level Design Elder"
msgstr "Anciano DiseñaNiveles"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Level Design Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_level_design_elder.dialogue:3
msgid ""
"[[Hi|Hello|Greetings]], StoryWeaver. Welcome to the wondrous world of level "
"design!"
msgstr ""
"[[Hola|Buenas|Saludos]], StoryWeaver. ¡Te doy la bienvenida al maravilloso "
"mundo del diseño de niveles!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Level Design Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_level_design_elder.dialogue:4
msgid ""
"If you've made it this far, I expect you have some imagination you are "
"itching to put to use."
msgstr ""
"Si has llegado hasta aquí, supongo que tienes algo de imaginación que te "
"mueres por poner en práctica."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Level Design Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_level_design_elder.dialogue:5
msgid ""
"These quests will show you some of the building blocks for creating your own "
"level."
msgstr ""
"Estas misiones te mostrarán algunos de los elementos básicos para crear tu "
"propio nivel."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Level Design Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_level_design_elder.dialogue:9
msgid "Very well, these will always be here when you need them."
msgstr "Muy bien, siempre estarán aquí para cuando las necesites."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Level Design Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_level_design_elder.dialogue:10
msgid "Good luck exploring the rest of the archipelago!"
msgstr "¡Buena suerte explorando el resto del archipiélago!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Level Design Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_level_design_elder.dialogue:12
msgid ""
"Excellent! Before you start messing about with mechanics, it's important to "
"have a well designed area for your adventure to take place."
msgstr ""
"¡Excelente! Antes de empezar a experimentar con las mecánicas, es importante "
"contar con una zona bien diseñada donde se desarrolle tu aventura."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Level Design Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_level_design_elder.dialogue:13
msgid ""
"Please let me know when you've put this to good use, I love seeing it work!"
msgstr ""
"Por favor, avísame cuando le hayas dado un buen uso, ¡me encantaría verla en "
"funcionamiento!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: Level Design Elder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_level_design_elder.dialogue:14
msgid "Some of Threadbare's finest quests use this!"
msgstr "¡Algunas de las mejores misiones de Threadbare la utilizan!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character name
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_repel_elder.dialogue
msgctxt "dialogue"
msgid "RepElder"
msgstr "Anciano Repelente"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: RepElder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_repel_elder.dialogue:3
msgid "[[Hi|Hello|Greetings]], StoryWeaver. I see you have decided to explore!"
msgstr "[[Hola|Buenas|Saludos]], StoryWeaver. ¡Veo que has decidido explorar!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: RepElder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_repel_elder.dialogue:4
msgid ""
"Oh, the sheep? They've been at this for hours, I'm tired just watching them."
msgstr "¿Ah, las ovejas? Llevan varias horas en eso, me cansa tan solo verlas."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: RepElder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_repel_elder.dialogue:5
msgid ""
"I wonder how they learned how to play like that... anyhow, repelling is a "
"skill everyone should try at least once."
msgstr ""
"Me pregunto cómo aprendieron a jugar así... en fin, el repeler es una "
"habilidad que todo el mundo debería probar al menos una vez."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: RepElder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_repel_elder.dialogue:9
msgid ""
"The archipelago is full of opportunities to play and be inventive. I trust "
"you will use it wisely."
msgstr ""
"El archipiélago está lleno de oportunidades para jugar y dar rienda suelta a "
"la inventiva. Confío en que las aprovecharás sabiamente."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: RepElder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_repel_elder.dialogue:10
msgid ""
"You don't find me repellent, do you? If you change your mind, my quests are "
"always available for you to practice."
msgstr ""
"No te resulto repulsivo, ¿verdad? Si cambias de opinión, mis misiones "
"siempre están disponibles para que practiques."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: RepElder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_repel_elder.dialogue:11
msgid ""
"Explore and have fun! I hope to see you again if you find yourself "
"forgetting how powerful repel can be."
msgstr ""
"¡Explora y diviértete! Espero volver a verte si alguna vez olvidas lo "
"poderoso que puede ser el repeler."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: RepElder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_repel_elder.dialogue:13
msgid "Nice one, that will certainly be fun to play with."
msgstr "Qué bien, seguro que será divertido jugar con eso."

#. TRANSLATORS: Character: RepElder
#: scenes/dev/components/dev_archipelago_repel_elder.dialogue:14
msgid "Good luck teaching the sheep how to do that!"
msgstr "¡Buena suerte enseñándoles a las ovejas a hacer eso!"

#: scenes/dev/dev_archipelago.tscn
msgid "Fray's End"
msgstr "Fray's End"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/enemy_interaction/gym_area/quest.tres
msgid "Gym Area"
msgstr "Área de gym"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/enemy_interaction/gym_area/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn how some legendary creatures like the Mothsache, StoryVore, and "
"InkDrinker behave when coexisting! "
msgstr ""
"¡Descubre cómo se comportan algunas criaturas legendarias, como el "
"Mothsache, el StoryVore y el InkDrinker al convivir!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/grapple/custom_hookable_objects/quest.tres
msgid "Custom Hookable Objects"
msgstr "Objetos enganchables custom"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/grapple/custom_hookable_objects/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn how you can use the grapple ability to interact with other objects in "
"the scene."
msgstr ""
"Aprende a utilizar la habilidad de gancho para interactuar con otros objetos "
"de la escena."

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/grapple_gym_1.tscn
msgid ""
"Can you go back the way you came? No? Sometimes grappling is asymmetric!"
msgstr ""
"¿Puedes volver por donde viniste? ¿No? A veces, ¡el enganche es asimétrico!"

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/grapple_gym_1.tscn
msgid ""
"Head to the next scene to experiment with grapple's reach and the longer "
"thread ability!"
msgstr ""
"¡Dirígete a la siguiente escena para experimentar con el alcance del gancho "
"y la habilidad de hilo largo!"

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/grapple_gym_1.tscn
msgid ""
"Hookable objects must be positioned at multiples of 45-degree angles. Notice "
"that the needle on the left is not accessible for keyboard-only users."
msgstr ""
"Los objetos enganchables se deben colocar en ángulos múltiplos de 45 grados. "
"Observa como la aguja de la izquierda no es accesible apuntando con el "
"teclado."

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/grapple_gym_1.tscn
msgid "Needles can be used to chain together a longer string."
msgstr "Se pueden conectar las agujas para conformar una cuerda más larga."

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/grapple_gym_1.tscn
msgid ""
"Position the pins carefully. The player may fall in water and get stuck!"
msgstr ""
"Coloca los alfileres con cuidado. ¡El jugador podría caer al agua y quedarse "
"atrapado!"

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/grapple_gym_1.tscn
msgid "Step on the dirt to change the color of your grapple string sprite!"
msgstr ""
"¡Pisa la tierra para cambiar el color del sprite de la cuerda de tu gancho!"

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/grapple_gym_1.tscn
msgid "Throw your grapple at hookable pins to get a boost!"
msgstr "¡Lanza tu gancho a los alfileres para engancharte e impulsarte!"

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/grapple_gym_1.tscn
msgid "You can even propel yourself across gaps!"
msgstr "¡Incluso puedes impulsarte para cruzar huecos!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/quest.tres
msgid "Grapple Gym (Basics)"
msgstr "Gym de enganche (fundamentos)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_1/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn some of the basics of the grappling mechanic. Crossing gaps, chaining "
"hookable needles, and changing the string's color."
msgstr ""
"Aprende algunos de los fundamentos de la mecánica de enganche: cruzar "
"huecos, conectar agujas y cambiar el color del hilo."

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_2/grapple_gym_2.tscn
msgid ""
"Test out your range with the grapple. It starts at 200 pixels by default, "
"but the size of the HookableArea makes each direction a little different."
msgstr ""
"Prueba el alcance del gancho. Por defecto es de 200 píxeles, pero el tamaño "
"del área de enganche (HookableArea) hace que cada dirección sea ligeramente "
"distinta."

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_2/grapple_gym_2.tscn
msgid ""
"Distances are based on the Player's global_position. The pins on sand are "
"one pixel out of reach!"
msgstr ""
"Las distancias se calculan a partir de la global_position del jugador. ¡Los "
"alfileres situados en la arena están a un píxel de distancia de poder "
"alcanzarlas!"

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_2/grapple_gym_2.tscn
msgid ""
"After getting the \"Longer Thread\" ability your grapple range increases! "
"The default range becomes 400 pixels."
msgstr ""
"¡Tras obtener la habilidad \"Hilo más largo\", el alcance de tu gancho "
"aumenta! El alcance predeterminado pasa a ser de 400 píxeles."

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_2/grapple_gym_2.tscn
msgid "You can reach further with the needle than the default grapple."
msgstr "Puedes llegar más lejos con la aguja que con el gancho predeterminado."

#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_2/grapple_gym_2.tscn
msgid "Chaining a set of needles together can be used to trigger events."
msgstr ""
"Al unir un conjunto de agujas puede utilizarse para desencadenar eventos."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_2/quest.tres
msgid "Grapple Gym (Reach and Longer Thread)"
msgstr "Gym de enganche (alcance e hilo más largo)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/grapple/grapple_gym_2/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn how far the grapple can reach with and without the Longer Thread "
"ability. Chain together sets of needles to trigger events. See how a needle "
"changes the reach of the grapple."
msgstr ""
"Descubre el alcance del gancho con y sin la habilidad \"Hilo más largo\". "
"Conecta grupos de agujas para activar eventos. Observa cómo una aguja "
"modifica el alcance del gancho."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/area_filler/interactive_area_filler_test.tscn
msgid ""
"Sometimes you want to decorate a large area without placing each scene by "
"hand."
msgstr ""
"A veces quieres decorar una zona amplia sin colocar cada escena manualmente."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/area_filler/interactive_area_filler_test.tscn
msgid ""
"Threadbare includes a tool called AreaFiller, which can automatically "
"populate an Area2D or StaticBody2D's shapes with scenes of your choosing."
msgstr ""
"Threadbare incluye una herramienta llamada AreaFiller, capaz de rellenar "
"automáticamente las formas de un Area2D o StaticBody2D con escenas de tu "
"elección."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/area_filler/interactive_area_filler_test.tscn
msgid ""
"Each interaction with this rock regenerates the field with a new selection "
"of flowers and mushrooms."
msgstr ""
"Cada interacción con esta roca regenera el campo con una nueva selección de "
"flores y hongos."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/area_filler/interactive_area_filler_test.tscn
msgid ""
"Each part of this field is covered by a CollisionPolygon2D shape, which is a "
"sibling of the AreaFiller node."
msgstr ""
"Cada parte de este campo está cubierta por una forma CollisionPolygon2D, que "
"es un nodo hermano del nodo AreaFiller."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/area_filler/interactive_area_filler_test.tscn
msgid ""
"Decrease (left) or increase (right) the space between each object, then go "
"back and redraw!"
msgstr ""
"¡Reduce (a la izquierda) o aumenta (a la derecha) el espacio entre cada "
"objeto, luego vuelve atrás y redibuja!"

#: scenes/dev/level_design/area_filler/interactive_area_filler_test.tscn
msgid ""
"The TreesPath Area2D is only used to hold the trees. It is set to not "
"collide with anything."
msgstr ""
"El Area2D TreesPath se utiliza únicamente para albergar los árboles. Está "
"configurada para no colisionar con nada."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/area_filler/interactive_area_filler_test.tscn
msgid ""
"This dense forest is a StaticBody2D, which prevents the player from walking "
"in between the trees even if they would fit."
msgstr ""
"Este bosque denso es un StaticBody2D, lo que impide que el jugador camine "
"entre los árboles, incluso si cabiera por el espacio."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/level_design/area_filler/quest.tres
msgid "Area Filler"
msgstr "Area Filler"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/level_design/area_filler/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn how to use Threadbare's AreaFiller tool to automatically fill large "
"areas with scenes of your choosing. Make a forest in seconds!"
msgstr ""
"Aprende a utilizar la herramienta AreaFiller de Threadbare para rellenar "
"automáticamente grandes áreas con las escenas que elijas. ¡Crea un bosque en "
"cuestión de segundos!"

#: scenes/dev/level_design/character_randomizer/character_randomizer_test.dialogue:3
msgid "Hey, I'm not just a random guy. I have a very unique seed number."
msgstr ""
"Oye, no soy una persona cualquiera. Tengo un número de semilla muy único."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/character_randomizer/character_randomizer_test.dialogue:6
msgid ""
"I'm blue! If you are happy with the random results, except for a thing..."
msgstr ""
"¡Soy azul! Si estás conforme con los resultados aleatorios, salvo por una "
"cosa..."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/character_randomizer/character_randomizer_test.dialogue:7
msgid ""
"...you can activate Editable Children and then reset the character seed to "
"zero. Then apply any changes to the inner nodes."
msgstr ""
"...puedes activar Hijos Editables y luego restablecer la semilla del "
"personaje a cero. Luego, aplica cualquier cambio a los nodos internos."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/character_randomizer/character_randomizer_test.dialogue:12
msgid "[[See you around.|Welcome to the town!]]"
msgstr "[[Nos vemos luego.|¡Que la pases bien en el pueblo!]]"

#: scenes/dev/level_design/character_randomizer/character_randomizer_test.tscn
msgid "townie_1"
msgstr "habitante_1"

#: scenes/dev/level_design/character_randomizer/character_randomizer_test.tscn
msgid "townie_2"
msgstr "habitante_2"

#: scenes/dev/level_design/character_randomizer/character_randomizer_test.tscn
msgid "townie_4"
msgstr "habitante_3"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/level_design/character_randomizer/quest.tres
msgid "Character Randomization"
msgstr "Aleatorización de personajes"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/level_design/character_randomizer/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn how to randomly generate townies from a variety of characteristics!"
msgstr ""
"¡Aprende a generar aleatoriamente habitantes de la ciudad a partir de una "
"variedad de características!"

#: scenes/dev/level_design/doors_and_levers/doors_and_levers.tscn
msgid "This lever is timed!"
msgstr "¡Esta manija está cronometrada!"

#: scenes/dev/level_design/doors_and_levers/doors_and_levers.tscn
msgid "Doesn't work by itself!"
msgstr "¡No funciona sola!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/level_design/doors_and_levers/quest.tres
msgid "Doors and Levers"
msgstr "Puertas y manijas"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/level_design/doors_and_levers/quest.tres
msgid "Play with doors and levers!"
msgstr "¡Juega con puertas y manijas!"

#: scenes/dev/level_design/time_and_weather/1_time_and_weather_museum.tscn
msgid "This is the current time. One minute in this scene is one day."
msgstr "Esta es la hora actual. Un minuto en esta escena equivale a un día."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/time_and_weather/1_time_and_weather_museum.tscn
msgid "Ligths turn on/off automatically."
msgstr "Las luces se prenden y apagan automáticamente."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/time_and_weather/1_time_and_weather_museum.tscn
msgid ""
"Check the behavior added to the light here, which makes it turn on/off "
"automatically."
msgstr ""
"Fíjate en el comportamiento añadido a la luz, que hace que se encienda y "
"apague automáticamente."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/time_and_weather/1_time_and_weather_museum.tscn
msgid ""
"The next scene will continue with the same time as this one. This is because "
"their TimeAndWeather nodes have the same setup."
msgstr ""
"La siguiente escena continuará a la misma hora que esta. Esto se debe a que "
"sus nodos TimeAndWeather tienen la misma configuración."

#: scenes/dev/level_design/time_and_weather/2_time_and_weather_museum.tscn
msgid ""
"Use rocks to set the time of day. Warning! This will unsync it with the "
"scene at west."
msgstr ""
"Usa las piedras para cambiar el horario. ¡Advertencia! Esto hará que se "
"desincronice con la escena del oeste."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/level_design/time_and_weather/quest.tres
msgid "Time and Weather"
msgstr "Tiempo y clima"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/level_design/time_and_weather/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn how to modify the time and weather within Threadbare. See how scenes "
"use lights when it is dark out."
msgstr ""
"Aprende a modificar la hora y el clima en Threadbare. Observa cómo las "
"escenas usan luces cuando está oscuro."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/playground/unify_abilities/quest.tres
msgid "Grapple + Repel Combo"
msgstr "Combo enganchar + repeler"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/playground/unify_abilities/quest.tres
msgid "Learn how to use both the grapple and repel mechanics at the same time."
msgstr ""
"Aprende a combinar las mecánicas de enganchar y repeler al mismo tiempo."

#: scenes/dev/repel/custom_repellable_objects/custom_repellable_objects_test.tscn
msgid "Repel the box to move it along the yellow carpet."
msgstr "Repele la caja para moverla a lo largo de la alfombra amarilla."

#: scenes/dev/repel/custom_repellable_objects/custom_repellable_objects_test.tscn
msgid "Bouncy balls! Can be repelled too."
msgstr "¡Pelotas de rebote! También se pueden repeler."

#: scenes/dev/repel/custom_repellable_objects/custom_repellable_objects_test.tscn
msgid "Repel the lever from this side to open the fence."
msgstr "Repele la palanca desde este lado para abrir el cerco."

#: scenes/dev/repel/custom_repellable_objects/custom_repellable_objects_test.tscn
msgid "This lever starts an automatic repel. Be careful!"
msgstr "Esta palanca activa un repeler automático. ¡Ten cuidado!"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/repel/custom_repellable_objects/quest.tres
msgid "Custom Repellable Objects"
msgstr "Objetos repelibles custom"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/repel/custom_repellable_objects/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Learn how you can use the repel ability to interact with other objects in "
"the scene."
msgstr ""
"Aprende a utilizar la habilidad de repeler para interactuar con otros "
"objetos de la escena."

#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/ink_combat_test.tscn
msgid ""
"InkDrinkers have consumed all ink and are using it to fire ink blobs at you! "
"Fill each barrel by repelling the projectiles into it."
msgstr ""
"¡Los InkDrinkers se han tragado toda la tinta y la están usando para "
"dispararte bolas de tinta! Llena cada barril repeliendo los proyectiles "
"hacia su interior."

#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/ink_combat_test.tscn
msgid "This enemy throws projectiles that move in a straight line."
msgstr "Este enemigo lanza proyectiles que se desplazan en línea recta."

#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/ink_combat_test.tscn
msgid "This enemy throws projectiles that follow you as you move."
msgstr "Este enemigo lanza proyectiles que te siguen mientras te mueves."

#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/ink_combat_test.tscn
msgid "Each barrel can require a different color!"
msgstr "¡Cada barril requiere un color diferente!"

#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/ink_combat_test.tscn
msgid ""
"Some barrels are fragile, the wrong color can crack them! You won't need all "
"3 to beat the section."
msgstr ""
"Algunos barriles son frágiles, ¡un color inadecuado hace que se rompan! No "
"necesitarás los tres para superar la sección."

#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/ink_combat_test.tscn
msgid ""
"Notice how the projectiles are thrown faster as more barrels are filled?"
msgstr ""
"¿Notas cómo los proyectiles se lanzan más rápido a medida que se llenan más "
"barriles?"

#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/ink_combat_test.tscn
msgid "These barrels must be filled in a particular order."
msgstr "Estos barriles deben llenarse en un orden determinado."

#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/ink_combat_test.tscn
msgid "Back to the start!"
msgstr "¡Volver a empezar!"

#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/ink_combat_test.tscn
msgid "Each section can be started and reset by repelling the lever."
msgstr "Cada sección puede iniciarse y reiniciarse repeliendo la palanca."

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest title
#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/quest.tres
msgid "Ink Combat"
msgstr "Combate de tinta"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest description
#: scenes/dev/repel/ink_combat/quest.tres
msgid ""
"Test your skills in ink combat in the Ink Drinker arena. Encounter fragile "
"barrels, sequential fills, and various projectiles!"
msgstr ""
"Pon a prueba tus habilidades de combate con tinta en la arena Ink Drinker. "
"¡Enfréntate a barriles frágiles, llenados secuenciales y diversos "
"proyectiles!"

